Package: Loupe2R
Type: Package
Title: Import 10x Genomics Visium '.cloupe' Files into Seurat Objects
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Niel", "Infante", email = "nielinfante@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Extracts count matrices, spatial coordinates, tissue images, UMAP
    embeddings, and cluster labels from 10x Genomics .cloupe files (including
    Visium HD) and imports them into Seurat objects via a Python extraction
    step (reticulate). Requires the Python package 'cloupe_extract' (not
    bundled; see 'SystemRequirements').
License: AGPL-3 + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2R
BugReports: https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2R/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    Seurat (>= 5.0.0),
    SeuratObject,
    methods,
    reticulate,
    png,
    jsonlite,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    arrow,
    digest,
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with the cloupe_extract package
    (https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2Py/tree/main/cloupe_extract),
    installed separately by the user, e.g. via 'pip install "cloupe_extract @
    git+https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2Py.git#subdirectory=cloupe_extract"'
    -- NOT bundled with or distributed by this R package. cloupe_extract pulls
    in numpy/scipy/Pillow itself and vendors its own copy of the .cloupe
    binary parser, so no further Python-side setup is needed. Installing
    'loupe2py' (the Python/AnnData sibling package) also installs
    cloupe_extract automatically, since loupe2py depends on it.
